SUMMARY:Walk the Eastern End of Maggie Valley Starting at McCracken Corner
  Park
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nMeet at McCracken Corner 
 Park\, 56 State Rd 1307\, Waynesville 28785 (Moody Farm Road/State Road 13
 07 intersects Soco Road twice\; this is the eastern intersection with a tr
 affic light further from Maggie Valley). We will meet at 2:00 p.m.\n\n**No
 te: There is no restroom at the start point. Our route will pass a conveni
 ence store\, and there is a restroom about halfway through the walk at Par
 ham Memorial Park. Please plan accordingly.**\n\nDress for the weather\; c
 onsider a hat and sunscreen. The walk is pretty flat\, all on pavement exc
 ept for a short portion near the end. Tennis shoes are fine\; walking pole
 s aren't needed (although I plan to bring one). Bring plenty of water and 
 a protein snack. Dogs are welcome. Strollers are fine.\n\nWe will walk up 
 Soco Road to Parham Memorial Park (the western intersection of Moody Farm 
 Road/State Road 1307 and Soco Road). Then we will walk along Moody Farm Ro
 ad\, with one short side excursion\, back to the start point.\n\nHope to s
 ee you there!
